  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program on Affirmative Finance Action for Women in Africa (AFAWA): Financing Climate Resilient Agricultural Practices in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme is an on-lending programme to provide credit lines to local banks. The loans will target micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) and farmer-based associations (FBAs) led by women to support low-emissions and climate-resilient agricultural practices.

&#x2022; It provides affirmative action financing for women-led MSMEs and FBAs to low-emissions climate-resilient agriculture practices, enabling women to access affordable credit.
&#x2022; It aims to catalyze private sector investment for climate resilient agricultural lending through a long-term financing by GCF.
&#x2022; GCF financing transforms the AE&#x2019;s gender initiative and the country&#x2019;s risk-sharing initiative in agriculture into a dedicated gender and climate resilient agriculture initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
